  "summary": "Webdav-O is a RAT used by Chinese APTs, primarily linked to TaskMasters and sharing code with tools from TA428. It is considered an evolution of the BlueTraveller/RemShell family. The malware uses Yandex.Disk for C2 via the WebDAV protocol, with commands and data encrypted using hardcoded or session-based RC4 keys. Webdav-O exists in both x86 and x64 versions and typically establishes persistence as a service.",
